2026-10-23T14:58:19.0993806Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1003678Z Switching to the Multi-user Installer
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1104902Z Welcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1115330Z 
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1116197Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1117014Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1117297Z 
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1118055Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1118780Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1119131Z 
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1119351Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1120120Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1120506Z 
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1121213Z 3. Create the system users (uids [30001..30008]) and groups (gid 30000)
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1122232Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1123354Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1124055Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1124433Z 
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1124925Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1125439Z 
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1125843Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1126598Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1126864Z 
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1127150Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1127460Z 
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1128043Z Would you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1128988Z No TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1131196Z 
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1131478Z I will:
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1132068Z 
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1132783Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1133958Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1134429Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1134880Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1135190Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1135504Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1135944Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1136343Z    /root
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1147415Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1148235Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1158382Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1159167Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1159453Z 
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1160250Z Ready to continue?
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1160661Z No TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1178355Z 
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1179069Z ---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1189022Z This script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1189809Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1190614Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1191028Z 
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1191337Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1191798Z 
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1192195Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1193234Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1193670Z 
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1193870Z If you would like to
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1194342Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1194546Z 
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1194782Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1195170Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1195357Z 
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1195366Z 
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1195629Z ~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1202098Z Before I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1202956Z been installed on this system.
2026-10-23T14:58:19.1247752Z 
